New finishes.

DBI to determine on site if structural is required.
Ok for DTI as per O. Luo, July 18th, 2025.

Field Review - Addition / Alteration - 3302 E 5th

Interior alterations to provide improvements and validate unauthorized work to this existing single detached house on this site.
Scope of work:
Remove unauthorized kitchen in the basement;
Infill one window on the basement south elevation;
Interior layout alterations;
Kitchen and washroom upgrades.

Related to
CF-2022-012749

OK for field review per O. Luo, Sep 24th, 2025

High Density Housing / Commercial - Addition / Alteration - Exterior alterations for envelope repair to this existing3-storey multiple dwelling building on this site. Scope of work includes:
- Replace all original stucco cladding (excluding existing rain screened areas);
- Replace all windows, sliding doors, patio doors (2) and skylights;
- Overcoat balcony liquid-applied membrane;
- Replace sloped and flat roofs;
- Repair concrete chimney caps, seal, and complete local brick repairs;
- Adding 2” of insulation at the north elevation only;
- Install new perforated aluminum soffits;
- Supply and install new vinyl fencing.

Notes:
1. Existing window, door, and skylight openings to remain the same sizes.
2. No interior or electrical work proposed. 
3. Any work other than building envelope repair/exterior work requires a separate permit.
4. Building Envelope Professional: Guillaume Vadeboncoeur at 604.533.2992. 
5. Permit reviewed and approved to VBBL #12511 (2019).

Field Review - Addition / Alteration - Exterior and interior alterations to provide improvements to this existing single detached home on this site. Scope of work includes interior wall and some window alterations, a new kitchen and laundry room on the main floor, and a wet bar in the lower floor. Filling the existing double height space on the second floor (No new FSR added) and removing the covered porch at the rear of the house.

OK for field review per O. Luo, June 5th, 2025.

Letter of assurance provided by:
Schedule B (Structural): Chungmo Chung, P.Eng., 604-469-3723

